"THE JOB:\nLINE 1: Fix the bug in src/sum.js so the tests in test/sum.test.js pass\nLINE 2: make npm test pass\n\nDestination (the only place the job may change files): docs/\n\nName ONLY a file the line asks to CHANGE (to fix, edit, write, add or remove). A file the line only says must pass, be read, be run or be checked (for example the tests it must make pass) is NOT a change: never name it. For EACH job line, for each file it asks to change, give the line number, the file path copied exactly from that line, and the folder that holds that file (the folder part of the path, ending with /). A line that names no file path to change is left out; never guess a path the line does not contain. Reply with JSON only, no prose, no code fence: {\"points\":[{\"line\":<line number>,\"file\":\"<path copied from the line>\",\"folder\":\"<its folder>\"}]}. Example: for the line \"LINE 1: Fix the bug in src/sum.js so the tests in test/sum.test.js pass\" the reply is {\"points\":[{\"line\":1,\"file\":\"src/sum.js\",\"folder\":\"src/\"}]}, and test/sum.test.js is not named because the line only needs those tests to pass; for \"LINE 2: make npm test pass\" it is {\"points\":[]}."
